    "https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13756": {
      "title": "Assistant/ Associate Professor - 3284",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Pembroke Applicant Portal | Assistant/ Associate Professor - 3284 Skip to Main Content UNCP home Human Resources Human Resources Visit Us Request Info Apply UNCP Home About UNC Pembroke Human Resources Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UNCP Home Contact Us Assistant/ Associate Professor - 3284 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Position Details Position Information Division Academic Affairs Department Social Work Working Title Assistant Professor of Social Work Vacancy Type Tenure Track Faculty Min T/E Requirements Degree in appropriate discipline area – prior experience teaching in higher education setting FTE 1 Recruitment Range Salary commensurate with education and experience Anticipated Hiring Range Salary commensurate with education and experience Position # 3284 FLSA Status Exempt Months per year 9 Is this a grant funded position? No If yes, please indicate the end date of the grant.(if applicable) N/A Primary Purpose of Organization Unit Social Work preparation Primary Purpose of Position Teaching 7 courses per academic year (courses may include field seminar and field supervision); developing curricula; providing academic advisement to current and prospective students; undertaking scholarship in area of expertise; serving on university and department committees; and providing services to communities/agencies within the region. Job Description The Department of Social Work at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke invites applications for one tenure-track 9-month faculty position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor. The Department of Social Work has both BSW and MSW programs. Programs include advanced standing, part-time and night/evening, and off-campus sites. The successful candidate may be required to teach across the BSW and MSW social work curricula, and field practicum. He/she will provide academic advisement, develop curriculum including on-line courses, and/or teach some courses at off-campus sites or in the evenings. In addition to instructional duties, he/she is required to maintain an active program of scholarship, participate in service activities, and be willing to seek and participate in extramural funding. This position will also coordinate the school social work licensure program. Rank is open and depends on the qualifications and achievements of the candidate, but no higher than the rank currently held at another university. Appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor is preferred. Qualifications: A Master of Social Work degree from a CSWE accredited institution is required but a doctoral degree in social work or closely related field is preferred, ABD will be considered; two years post MSW work experience; college/university teaching experience; willingness to teach at off-campus sites; ability to teach online will be an asset. Expectations: The successful candidate may be required to teach one or more areas of the BSW and MSW social work curricula, and field practicum. He/she will provide academic advisement, develop curriculum including on-line courses, and/or teach some courses at off-campus sites and/or online. In addition to instructional duties, he/she will be is required to participate in university and departmental committees and provide community services. Online applications should be submitted through UNC -Pembroke Human Resource website. Application should include: 1. A cover letter indicating relevant professional work experience, college/university teaching experiences, teaching philosophy, and research interests. 2. A current CV with the names and contact information, including email address for at least 3 references. 3. Unofficial academic transcripts (scan copies and attach to your online application). Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. Contact: Dr. Alice Kay Locklear, Search Committee Chair Department of Social Work University of North Carolina at Pembroke 1 University Drive, PO Box 1510 Pembroke, NC 28372 Management Preference A doctoral degree in social work or closely related field is preferred but candidates who are currently ABD in a social work or closely related doctoral programs would be considered. Ability and/or willingness to teach in-person and online courses and teach across BSW and MSW curricula. School social work practice experience or licensure. Lic or Certification required by statute or regulation Posting Information Job Opening Date 09/30/2026 Job Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Category Faculty Posting Number EPA01175 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13755 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Applicant Documents Required Documents C V/Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 Other Document 4 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13741": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice - 3419",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Pembroke Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice - 3419 Skip to Main Content UNCP home Human Resources Human Resources Visit Us Request Info Apply UNCP Home About UNC Pembroke Human Resources Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UNCP Home Contact Us Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice - 3419 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Position Details Position Information Division Academic Affairs Department Sociology & Criminal Jus. Working Title Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice - 3419 Vacancy Type Tenure Track Faculty Min T/E Requirements Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or Sociology (with a concentration in Criminal Justice or Criminology) required. ABD with Ph.D. completed by date of appointment will be considered. FTE 1 Recruitment Range Commensurate Upon Education and Experience Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate Upon Education and Experience Position # 3419 FLSA Status Exempt Months per year 9 Is this a grant funded position? No If yes, please indicate the end date of the grant.(if applicable) n/a Primary Purpose of Organization Unit Teaching, service, scholarship, and research. Primary Purpose of Position Teaching, service, scholarship, and research. Job Description The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor of Sociology and Criminal Justice position to begin in the fall of 2027. The University of North Carolina at Pembroke is one of the seventeen member institutions in the University of North Carolina system. The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice is growing in size and offers numerous opportunities for creative teaching, including on-line courses, as well as advancement of scholarship. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach undergraduate Criminal Justice courses, both online and in the classroom. Courses can include Introduction to Criminal Justice, Criminology, and possibly Social Statistics and Social Research. There will also be opportunities to teach upper level and graduate level courses, and possibly Sociology classes. Teach Writing Intensive courses. Develop and deliver engaging instruction using various teaching modalities Provide academic advising and mentorship to undergraduate students Maintain an active research agenda in the discipline Participate actively in university service, including committee work, curriculum development and campus initiatives. Apply discipline-specific skills towards community-engagement with the local community and region. Contribute to a supportive learning environment that promotes student achievement and academic excellence · Applicant Instructions : Please attach cover letter of interest, CV and list of at least three professional references with contact information which includes phone number and email address. Management Preference Ability to teach undergraduate Social Statistics Prefer an individual capable and willing to teach both sociology and criminal justice courses. Experience in online instruction at the University level preferred. Lic or Certification required by statute or regulation Posting Information Job Opening Date 08/04/2026 Job Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Category Faculty Posting Number EPA01162 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13582 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Applicant Documents Required Documents C V/Resume Cover Letter Other Document Optional Documents Other Document 2 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Agency Referral American Librarian Association (ALA) Association of Fundraising Professionals BlacksInHigherEd.com Career Builder Chronicle of Higher Education Cosida CUPA HR Disabled in Higher Ed Disability Website (Other) Educause Glassdoor HigherEdJobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed Journal of Blacks in Higher Education LinkedIn Monster NACUBO NativeAmericansInHigherEd.com Native Hire NCAA Market NC Works Online / One Stop Center Newspaper Personal Referral Placement Exchange SACUBO Society of Human Resources Management (SHRM) StudentAffairs.com UNC Collaborative Website UNC Pembroke Online Employment System Veterans Advantage Jobs & Career Network Veteran Website (Other) VeteransInHigherEd.com Vocational Rehab Women in Higher Education Website - Other * Do you have experience teaching in a higher education environment? If so, please explain on your application or via your CV/Resume. Yes No CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
