    "https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13724": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - 2479",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Pembroke Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor - 2479 Skip to Main Content UNCP home Human Resources Human Resources Visit Us Request Info Apply UNCP Home About UNC Pembroke Human Resources Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UNCP Home Contact Us Assistant Professor - 2479 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Position Details Position Information Division Academic Affairs Department Management, International Business and Supply Chain Management (MIBS) Working Title Assistant Professor of Management Vacancy Type Tenure Track Faculty Min T/E Requirements Degree in appropriate discipline area – prior experience teaching in higher education setting FTE 1 Recruitment Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Position # 2479 FLSA Status Exempt Months per year 9 Is this a grant funded position? No If yes, please indicate the end date of the grant.(if applicable) N/A Primary Purpose of Organization Unit The Thomas College of Business and Economics at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke prepares students to become knowledgeable, ethical, innovative, and effective business professionals who are equipped to succeed in a dynamic and increasingly global business environment. The College is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business ( AACSB ), reflecting its commitment to academic quality, rigor, relevance, engagement, and continuous improvement. The Thomas College of Business and Economics emphasizes student success through energetic and engaging instruction, effective business communication, experiential learning, professional and career readiness, ethical decision-making, leadership development, global awareness, and the application of contemporary business practices. The College seeks to connect classroom learning with real-world business challenges while developing students’ abilities to communicate effectively, work collaboratively, lead others, think critically, and make sound business decisions. Through innovative teaching, scholarship, service, and engagement with the business community, the College prepares students to succeed in rapidly changing professional environments and to effectively utilize emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, as responsible and productive business professionals. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to provide energetic, engaging, and contemporary instruction in Business Communication at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with the ability to teach Management and related business courses as needed. The position will emphasize the development of students’ written, oral, interpersonal, presentation, and professional communication skills necessary for success in today’s workplace. The faculty member will use innovative and experiential teaching approaches that connect classroom learning with real-world business situations and promote professional and career readiness. Instruction should incorporate contemporary business practices and emerging technologies, including the appropriate use of artificial intelligence and other communication technologies. The position will also contribute to teaching in related areas such as organizational behavior, international business, leadership, professional development, and other Management disciplines based on the needs of the College. The position includes scholarship, service, student engagement, and other responsibilities consistent with the mission of the Thomas College of Business and Economics and the expectations of the University. Job Description On-campus and online delivery of undergraduate and graduate courses in Management with a primary emphasis on Business Management; scholarship in Management with a primary emphasis on Business Management service to the university, profession, and broader community; and other forms of organizational citizenship behavior for the betterment of the university and key stakeholders. On an ongoing basis, the successful candidate must publish in discipline-appropriate peer-reviewed journals to maintain AACSB Scholarly Academic (SA) status and for tenure and promotion consideration. Beyond scholarship, service to the University/School/Department and the business community is valued and required. Accordingly, performance will be assessed based on teaching, research, and service quality. Rank is open and commensurate with education and experience. App instructions: attach copies of transcripts, a reference list, and contact information. Management Preference Higher education teaching experience, with preference for experience teaching Business Communication, Management, or related business courses. Preference for candidates who demonstrate an energetic, engaging, and contemporary teaching approach; experience with experiential and applied learning; and the ability to incorporate emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, into instruction. Experience teaching in both face-to-face and online environments is preferred. Lic or Certification required by statute or regulation None Posting Information Job Opening Date 09/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Category Faculty Posting Number EPA01171 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13723 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Applicant Documents Required Documents C V/Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document Other Document 2 Other Document 3 Other Document 4 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Agency Referral American Librarian Association (ALA) Association of Fundraising Professionals BlacksInHigherEd.com Career Builder Chronicle of Higher Education Cosida CUPA HR Disabled in Higher Ed Disability Website (Other) Educause Glassdoor HigherEdJobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed Journal of Blacks in Higher Education LinkedIn Monster NACUBO NativeAmericansInHigherEd.com Native Hire NCAA Market NC Works Online / One Stop Center Newspaper Personal Referral Placement Exchange SACUBO Society of Human Resources Management (SHRM) StudentAffairs.com UNC Collaborative Website UNC Pembroke Online Employment System Veterans Advantage Jobs & Career Network Veteran Website (Other) VeteransInHigherEd.com Vocational Rehab Women in Higher Education Website - Other CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
