nd seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Position Details Position Information Division Academic Affairs Department Accounting, Finance & Information Technology Management (AFIT) Working Title Business Law Adjunct (2026-2027) Vacancy Type Part-Time Temporary Min T/E Requirements Applicants with a J.D. and experience in healthcare law and online teaching will receive the highest priority. J.D. holders with professional experience will be seriously considered. FTE .5 Recruitment Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Anticipated Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Number of vacancies 4 Position # ADJB02 FLSA Status Exempt Months per year 4 Work Schedule =e.g. 8-500 20 hours/week, flexible schedule Work Schedule Type Flexible Primary Purpose of Organization Unit Primary Purpose of Position Instruction of Students taking Business Law courses. Job Description The Department of Accounting and Finance commonly has the need for a part-time faculty to teach Business Law & Ethics courses in the 2026-2027 academic year. Teach online/ face-to-face, graduate/undergraduate level courses in business law such as legal and ethical issues, legal issues for managers, legal and ethical issues for health care professionals, international business law etc. The Accounting, Finance & Information Technology Management Department has a strong commitment to undergraduate/graduate teaching and part-time faculty are expected to exhibit and maintain campus and department standards. Work Location: Main campus of the University of North Carolina at Pembroke. Applicant Instructions: Please include copies of your transcripts, cover letter, and CV. Management Preference Online teaching experience is required. Proven and documented success in undergraduate/graduate teaching is highly desirable. Lic or Certification required by statute or regulation Posting Information Job Opening Date 07/20/2026 Job Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Cat