pression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Position Details Position Information Division Academic Affairs Department Chemistry & Physics Working Title Assistant Professor of Analytical and Forensic Chemistry Vacancy Type Tenure Track Faculty Min T/E Requirements Degree in appropriate discipline area – prior experience teaching in higher education setting FTE 1 Recruitment Range Salary commensurate with education and experience Anticipated Hiring Range Salary commensurate with education and experience Position # 888 FLSA Status Exempt Months per year 9 Is this a grant funded position? No If yes, please indicate the end date of the grant.(if applicable) N/A Primary Purpose of Organization Unit Chemistry and Physics Unit Primary Purpose of Position To teach chemistry Job Description The Department of Chemistry & Physics at the University of North Carolina at Pembroke invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Analytical and Forensic Chemistry position beginning August 2027. UNC Pembroke is a student-centered public university with a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and research. We seek a dynamic educator-scholar committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentoring, and the development of a vibrant research program that engages undergraduate students in meaningful scholarly experiences. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching, student mentoring, and scholarly activity. Responsibilities include: Teaching undergraduate courses in analytical chemistry (lecture and laboratory), instrumental analysis, forensic chemistry, general chemistry, and other courses that support departmental needs and align with the candidate’s expertise. Developing and maintaining an active research program that provides hands-on research opportunities for undergraduate students. Overseeing, maintaining, and integrating modern analytical instrumentation into teaching and research activities. Contributing to departmental, university, and professional service activities. Demonstrating a commitment to fostering an inclusive learning environment and supporting the academic success of students from diverse backgrounds. Qualifications Required Ph.D. in Analytical Chemistry or a closely related field. Academic preparation and expertise sufficient to teach undergraduate analytical chemistry, forensic chemistry, and instrumental analysis. Demonstrated experience with the operation, maintenance, and application of modern analytical instrumentation. Preferred Prior undergraduate teaching experience. Demonstrated commitment to effective teaching and mentoring of undergraduate students. Willingness to develop forensic chemistry courses for chemistry majors and interdisciplinary forensic science courses for non-majors. Experience incorporating undergraduate students into research activities. Application Materials Applicants should submit: A cover letter describing interest in the position and qualifications. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy. A research statement outlining plans for establishing and maintaining an undergraduate research program. A statement describing the candidate’s approach to supporting student success, mentoring, and creating an inclusive learning environment. Contact information for three professional references. Review of Applications Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Early application is encouraged. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of North Carolina at Pembroke is an equal opportunity employer Management Preference Ph.D. in Analytical Chemistry Prior undergraduate teaching experience and mentoring undergraduate students in research Lic or Certification required by statute or regulation Posting Information Job Opening Date 10/16/2026 Job Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Category Faculty Posting Number EPA01186 Quick Link to Posting https://jobs.uncp.edu/postings/13827 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. New employees are paid only by direct deposit to the financial institution of their choice. Candidates claiming Veterans Preference must attach a copy of their DD-214 as a part of the online application process. UNC Pembroke is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against qualified individuals based on their status as protected veterans or individuals with disabilities, and prohibits discrimination against all individuals based on their age, race, color, genetic information, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression and national origin. UNC Pembroke is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Applicant Documents Required Documents C V/Resume Cover Letter Other Document Other Document 2 Optional Documents Other Document 3 Other Document 4 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Agency Referral American Librarian Association (ALA) Association of Fundraising Professionals BlacksInHigherEd.com Career Builder Chronicle of Higher Education Cosida CUPA HR Disabled in Higher Ed Disability Website (Other) Educause Glassdoor HigherEdJobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed Journal of Blacks in Higher Education LinkedIn Monster NACUBO NativeAmericansInHigherEd.com Native Hire NCAA Market NC Works Online / One Stop Center Newspaper Personal Referral Placement Exchange SACUBO Society of Human Resources Management (SHRM) StudentAffairs.com UNC Collaborative Website UNC Pembroke Online Employment System Veterans Advantage Jobs & Career Network Veteran Website (Other) VeteransInHigherEd.com Vocational Rehab Women in Higher Education Website - Other CAMPUS DIRECTORY | ASK UNCP | UNIVERSITY CALENDAR To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
